{"key":"CgmWindow","text":"## CgmWindow\n\nThe **CGM Window** is a glucose dashboard. Connect a Dexcom account and it\nshows your latest reading with its trend arrow, a trace of the last few hours\nagainst your target range, and the summary numbers clinicians use (time in\nrange, mean, variability, GMI).\n\n---\n\n@layout\nBig Readout | 0.50, 0.18 | The newest reading, its unit, the Dexcom trend arrow, and how old the reading is. The age turns amber once a reading is more than 15 minutes old.\nSummary Tiles | 0.50, 0.36 | In range, below, above, mean, variability (CV), GMI and the last 15 minutes. Hover a tile for what it means.\nChart | 0.50, 0.66 | The trace for the chosen span. The shaded band is the 70 to 180 target range; the red line is urgent low. Out-of-range readings are colored dots and the newest point is ringed. Gaps longer than 15 minutes break the line.\nFooter | 0.50, 0.95 | Connection status on the left, then the environment, span, unit, refresh and Connect or Disconnect buttons.\n\n---\n\n### Connecting\n\n- **Connect** — opens a Dexcom sign-in page in a new browser tab. The window waits for you to finish (up to ten minutes), then starts retrieving readings.\n- **Disconnect** — forgets the link. Nothing about your Dexcom login is stored in the layout file.\n- **sandbox / production** — which Dexcom environment the next Connect uses. Production requires Dexcom's approval of the app; sandbox serves demo data.\n- Readings refresh automatically every minute; press **↻** to fetch now.\n\n### Controls\n\n- **Span** — click the hours button to cycle 3, 6, 12 and 24 hours\n- **Unit** — click mg/dL to switch the display to mmol/L; stored values stay in mg/dL\n- **Right-click the title bar** — Connect or Disconnect, choose the environment, or Save and Export\n\n### Saving\n\n- **Save to GitHub** writes the readings as a CSV file (utc, mg_dl, mmol_l, trend) under Files/CGM in your account folder\n- **Export** downloads the same CSV\n\n### Shortcuts\n\n- Button-driven; no special keys.\n\n### Status: Beta\n### Purpose: OS\n\n---","screenshot":""}